WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360
Ragda Pattice comes from Mumbai, in the state
of Maharashtra, on India's western coast.

00:01:27.174 --> 00:01:39.174
It grew up as part of Mumbai's street-food culture
through the twentieth century, and while nobody can say
for certain who first put ragda and pattice on the
same plate, it has gone on to become one of
India's best-loved vegetarian snacks.

00:02:54.349 --> 00:03:06.349
At its base is ragda — white peas simmered in
Indian spices for plant-based protein, fibre and iron —
paired with pattice, golden potato patties that bring
carbohydrates and energy to the plate.

00:04:21.523 --> 00:04:33.523
Finished with fresh onions, coriander, mint chutney, sweet
tamarind chutney and a scattering of crunchy sev, the
whole dish brings together protein, fibre, vitamins and
energy in one bowl.

00:05:48.697 --> 00:05:55.517
Ragda Pattice is loved for its perfect balance of
spicy, sweet, tangy and crunchy flavours.

00:07:15.871 --> 00:07:27.871
It is affordable, filling and satisfying — the combination
of hot ragda, crispy potato patties and fresh chutneys
makes it a favourite street food for people of all ages.

00:08:43.046 --> 00:08:50.316
More than just a snack, Ragda Pattice represents the
rich tradition of Indian vegetarian street food.
